_delay":367.46,"q90_delay":589.8000000000002,"undetected":0},{"adversary":"coupled_stealth_shift","max_delay":1127,"mean_delay":471.76,"q90_delay":717.7000000000003,"undetected":0}]},"e_process":"equal-weight mixture of five exact likelihood-ratio martingales","fractional_worst_mean_improvement":0.11306913718637703,"null_alarms":0,"null_replays":500,"photon_budget":8000,"replay_trials_per_alternative":100,"worst_mean_optimized":538.03,"worst_mean_uniform":606.62},"status":"PASS","theorem":"For the declared five-family audit model, pilot allocation is a finite minimax experiment-design problem. The optimal predictable allocation assigns approximately 30.46 percent of photons to the reference interferometer, 33.49 percent to the dark monitor, 18.21 percent to joint pair pilots, and 17.85 percent to the shadow sentinel. It raises the worst-case KL information from 0.0135246 to 0.0163225 nats per photon, a 20.69 percent gain. An equal-weight mixture likelihood-ratio e-process retains a rigorous 0.001 anytime false-alarm bound. In deterministic replays the optimized design reduces the worst mean detection delay from 606.62 to 538.03 photons and detects every simulated alternative within budget."}
